INT. SUNDERLY'S HOARD - INSIDE A DRAGON'S TOOTH - NIGHT

A hollow in an ancient fang, wide as a cottage. Gold coins pile up like dunes in the dark. Dragon breath stirs the air, warm, sulfurous.

GRETEL VOSS, 20s, soot-streaked, sword drawn, edges toward a chalice on a gilt pillar. Behind her, in the dark beyond the tooth, SUNDERLY, a dragon, enormous, ancient, amused. Only its voice and an amber eye show.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
Little thief. You are in my tooth.

GRETEL
I noticed.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
It is the one that hurts.

GRETEL
I'm sorry.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
You are not sorry. You are armed.

GRETEL
Both can be true.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
Show me the sword.

Gretel lifts the blade. It trembles. She lowers it.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
Show me the other thing in your pocket.

GRETEL
There is no other thing.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
There is always another thing.

She pulls a small iron pick from her coat.

GRETEL
For the tooth.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
You came to pull my tooth?

GRETEL
I came for the chalice. The pick was for the lock. But the tooth is rotten. I can fix it.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
If I let you.

GRETEL
If you let me.

Silence. The amber eye blinks, slow as a sunrise.

SUNDERLY (O.S.)
Then do it quickly.

GRETEL ^
Then hold still.

She wedges the pick into the black cavity. The tooth cracks. A scream of dragon, a quake in the gold, and a coin avalanche that buries her to the knees. She laughs, spitting coins.
